Done. Issue #22 is implemented and committed on `fp/22-1-1-dialogs-ts-module` (6b9624c, not pushed).

**What was added:**
- `src/lib/dialogs.ts` — the single dialog choke point per plan 01 §3:
  - `pickOpenFile()` → multi-select open dialog, markdown filters by default, optional custom filters/title (for DOCX import later)
  - `pickOpenFolder()` → native directory dialog
  - `pickSavePath(defaultName, filter, title?)` → save dialog seeded with `defaultPath`
  - `confirmMessage({title, message, kind, buttons})` → native message dialog with `ok`/`okCancel`/`yesNo`/`yesNoCancel`, normalized to a `MessageResult`
  - Filters: `MARKDOWN_FILTER` (md/markdown/mdown/mkd), `DOCX_FILTER`, `extensionFilter()` for per-format export
  - Tauri branch uses `@tauri-apps/plugin-dialog` (dynamic import, matching the `Explorer.tsx` convention); browser branch falls back to `window.prompt`/`confirm`/`alert`
- `src/lib/__tests__/dialogs.test.ts` — 20 vitest tests: browser-mode fallback selection logic returns the simulated `prompt`/`confirm`/`alert` values (including cancel/dismiss → `null`/`"no"`/`"cancel"`), and Tauri wrappers verified via `@tauri-apps/api/mocks` `mockIPC` (correct `plugin:dialog|open|save|message` commands, forwarded options, result normalization)

